  "title": "Turán number of a finite family.",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Given a finite family ${\\cal F}$ of graphs and an integer $n$, the Turán number $ex(n,{\\cal F})$ of ${\\cal F}$ is the largest integer $m$ such that there exists a graph on $n$ vertices with $m$ edges which contains no member of ${\\cal F}$ as a subgraph.\n\nConjecture For every finite family ${\\cal F}$ of graphs there exists an $F\\in {\\cal F}$ such that $ex(n, F ) = O(ex(n, {\\cal F}))$.",
